# File Size Rule: ≤ 200 Lines

Every TypeScript/TSX file in this project MUST stay under **200 lines** of code (excluding blank lines and comments).

## When a file approaches or exceeds 200 lines:

1. **Split by responsibility** — extract sub-components, helper functions, or hooks into separate files
2. **Co-locate the split** — keep related files in the same folder
3. **Create a barrel** — use `index.ts` to re-export from the folder

## Splitting strategies:

| Scenario | Solution |
|----------|----------|
| Large component with sub-components | Extract each sub-component to its own file |
| Component with heavy logic | Extract logic into `use<Name>.ts` hook |
| File with many type definitions | Move types to `<name>.types.ts` |
| File with many constants | Move constants to `<name>.constants.ts` |
| File with utility functions | Move to `utils/<name>.ts` |

## Examples

**Bad** — one 300-line component file:
```
components/shared/data-display/DataTable.tsx  (300 lines)
```

**Good** — split into focused files:
```
components/shared/data-display/
  DataTable.tsx           (main component, <100 lines)
  DataTableHeader.tsx     (header sub-component)
  DataTablePagination.tsx (pagination sub-component)
  useDataTable.ts         (table logic hook)
  data-table.types.ts     (type definitions)
  index.ts                (barrel exports)
```

## Enforcement

Before creating or editing any file, count existing lines. If adding code would push it over 200 lines, split first, then add.
